Network Monitoring Tools
Nagios Setup
1. Installation

    sudo dnf install nagios - Install Nagios core
    
    sudo dnf install nagios-plugins-all - Install monitoring plugins

2. Service Management

    sudo systemctl start nagios - Start Nagios service
    
    sudo systemctl enable nagios - Enable auto-start

3. Web Interface

    Access: http://your-server/nagios
    
    Default credentials: nagiosadmin / (set during installation)

4. Configuration

    Configuration files: /etc/nagios/
    
    Define hosts, services, and notifications

Zabbix Setup
1. Installation

    sudo dnf install https://repo.zabbix.com/zabbix/5.4/rhel/8/x86_64/zabbix-release-5.4-1.el8.noarch.rpm - Add Zabbix repository
    
    sudo dnf install zabbix-server-mysql zabbix-web-mysql zabbix-appliance - Install Zabbix components

2. Database Setup

    sql
    CREATE DATABASE zabbix CHARACTER SET utf8 COLLATE utf8_bin;
    CREATE USER 'zabbix'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED BY 'your_password';
    GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON zabbix.* TO 'zabbix'@'localhost';
    zcat /usr/share/doc/zabbix-server-mysql*/create.sql.gz | mysql -uzabbix -p zabbix - Import schema

3. Configuration

    sudo nano /etc/zabbix/zabbix_server.conf - Set database password
    
    sudo systemctl start zabbix-server zabbix-agent httpd - Start services
    
    sudo systemctl enable zabbix-server zabbix-agent httpd - Enable auto-start

4. Web Interface

    Access: http://your-server/zabbix
    
    Default credentials: Admin / zabbix

System and Network Performance Tuning
1. System Updates

    sudo dnf update - Keep system updated

2. Performance Monitoring

    top, htop, glances - Monitor system resources
    
    Identify CPU, memory, and disk bottlenecks

3. Memory Optimization

    sudo nano /etc/sysctl.conf - Add: vm.swappiness = 10
    
    sudo sysctl -p - Apply changes (reduces swap usage)

4. Filesystem Optimization

    fstab options: noatime,nodiratime - Reduce disk writes
    
    SSD Trim: sudo systemctl enable fstrim.timer - Enable periodic TRIM

5. Kernel Tuning

      /etc/sysctl.conf modifications:
      
      net.core.somaxconn - Increase connection queue
      
      net.core.netdev_max_backlog - Improve network buffer
      
      net.ipv4.tcp_max_syn_backlog - Enhance TCP performance

6. File Limits

    sudo nano /etc/security/limits.conf:

    text
    * soft nofile 65535
    * hard nofile 65535
    sudo nano /etc/security/limits.d/20-nproc.conf - Adjust process limits

7. Service Management

    sudo systemctl disable service-name - Disable unnecessary services

    Free up system resources

8. Filesystem Selection

    Consider XFS or Btrfs for performance
    
    Choose based on workload requirements

Network Troubleshooting
1. Basic Connectivity Checks

    nmcli or ip a - Check interface status and IP addresses
    
    ping -c 4 8.8.8.8 - Test internet connectivity
    
    ping -c 4 gateway-ip - Test local network connectivity

2. DNS Resolution

    cat /etc/resolv.conf - Check DNS servers
    
    cat /etc/nsswitch.conf - Verify resolution order
    
    dig example.com or nslookup example.com - Test DNS resolution

3. Firewall Verification

    sudo firewall-cmd --list-all - View current rules
    
    sudo firewall-cmd --add-service=http --permanent - Allow services as needed
    
    sudo firewall-cmd --reload - Apply changes

4. Service Restarts

    sudo systemctl restart NetworkManager - Restart network manager
    
    sudo systemctl restart network - Alternative restart command

5. Physical Connectivity

    Check network cables and physical connections
    
    Verify switch/router ports are active
    
    Test with different network connection

6. Security Services

    setenforce 0 - Temporarily disable SELinux for testing
    
    Check host-based firewall rules

7. Log Analysis

    tail -f /var/log/messages - System messages
    
    journalctl -xe - Systemd journal
    
    dmesg - Kernel messages

8. Configuration Validation

    Review /etc/sysconfig/network-scripts/ifcfg-* - Interface configurations
    
    Check /etc/sysconfig/network - Global network settings
    
    Verify /etc/hosts - Local hostname resolution

9. Routing Issues

    ip route show - View routing table
    
    traceroute google.com - Trace network path

10. DHCP Problems
    - Check DHCP server availability
    - Verify lease pools and timing
    - Review /var/log/messages for DHCP errors

11. Final Resolution
    - Server reboot if issues persist
    - Check for IP address conflicts
    - Verify network hardware functionality
